.Dd November 3, 2026
.Dt MK.VCVARSALL.MK 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mk.vcvarsall.mk
.Nd finds MSVC without a developer prompt
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Does what
.Pa vcvarsall.bat
does, so
.Va TOOLCHAIN Ns = Ns Cm msvc
works from a plain Cygwin shell.
It finds a toolset and Windows SDK in a mounted EWDK if one is named, otherwise
through
.Pa vswhere.exe ,
and sets the
.Ev PATH ,
.Ev INCLUDE
and
.Ev LIB
they need.
It is skipped for a
.Fl V
query and
.Cm clean .
.Pp
Not included directly by a makefile.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "BMK_EWDK_ROOT"
.It Ev BMK_EWDK_ROOT
Where an EWDK ISO is mounted, in Windows or Cygwin form:
.Pa F:\e
or
.Pa /cygdrive/f .
No Visual Studio is needed then.
.El
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Bl -diag
.It TOOLCHAIN=msvc: BMK_EWDK_ROOT= Ns Ar dir has no ... BuildTools
The ISO is not mounted there.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mk.toolchain.msvc.mk 5 ,
.Xr bmake-it 7
.Sh AUTHORS
.An Sylvain Souche
